  "notes": [
    "16 offices, 16 people, 0 vacancies -- 11 city, 5 county. Zero reuses: all 16 external_ids are fresh inserts (production measured 2026-09-01, the sub-range holds 0 rows).",
    "ONE government with THREE chambers. Columbus is the program's first consolidated city-county, so stage 4 drops the county commission -- the Council already is it -- and keeps only the separately elected county officers.",
    "Ruling R1: the Council is 8 district councilors + 2 at-large (Posts 9 and 10), charter Sec. 3-100(2) and 3-100(3). Both GIS layers return 8 polygons, which independently confirms the at-large pair has no geometry. The city's roster page numbers all ten 'District N' and would have produced two districts that do not exist.",
    "Ruling R2: the Mayor is voting_powers 'non_voting' with a required representation_note. CORRECTED CITATION -- the Mayor's powers are charter Sec. 4-201(2) and 4-201(4), NOT Sec. 4-102. Sec. 4-102 is 'General provisions concerning departments'. ROSTERS.md, ga.md and the plan all cite 4-102 and the charter text on disk does not support it.",
    "Ruling R3: Mayor Pro Tem is a parenthetical, not an office. Sec. 3-103(1): the Council elects one of its own members by six votes, annually. The post-verify gate refuses any office titled with it.",
    "Ruling R4: 5 county officers -- Sheriff, Clerk of Superior Court, Judge of Probate Court, Tax Commissioner, Coroner. Charter Art. VIII Ch. 1 'County Officers and Agencies' preserves four (Sec. 8-100, 8-101, 8-102, 8-103); the Clerk of Superior Court comes in via Ga. Const. Art. IX, Sec. I, Par. III. Muscogee elects no Marshal and no Surveyor, so Baldwin's six-officer template does NOT transfer. Both municipal-court offices are excluded (Cantrell, 2026-09-01).",
    "how_started 'special election' IS NOT A LEGAL VALUE. essentials.office_terms carries CHECK how_started IN ('elected','appointed','succeeded','redistricted','unknown'). Barnes and Cook won SPECIAL elections, so how_started is 'elected' and the special-election fact is carried in the source string and the migration header, not in the column. The plan's Task 3 text says 'special election' and would fail that CHECK.",
    "Party is deliberately absent. It lives on races.primary_party, never on a person or an office.",
    "District types differ by tier: CITY districts are district_type 'LOCAL', COUNTY districts are 'COUNTY'. The citywide LOCAL district IS created here; the countywide COUNTY district is only ASSERTED -- the TIGER county load already made 13215/G4020, verified in production 2026-09-01."
  ],
